2	LEPT-2026-1	LEPT PRE-TEST 1	\N	{"settings": {"endDate": "", "endTime": "", "fontSize": 14, "startDate": null, "startTime": null, "fontFamily": "'Inter', sans-serif", "maxRetries": 0, "isAssignment": false, "referencePdf": null, "referencePdfs": [], "timeLimitMinutes": 0}, "questions": [{"id": "q_1789319019091_11_3dtzpbl", "text": "The measure of location which is the most likely to be influenced by extreme values in the data set is the", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_11_A_sob3_uazg", "text": "range", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_11_B_ybxb_4tos", "text": "median", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_11_C_73ln_y1n0", "text": "mode", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_11_D_pc9m_dd9v", "text": "mean", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_12_noeipnx", "text": "If two events are independent, then", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_12_A_nqnw_tvtd", "text": "they must be mutually exclusive", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_12_B_jgz1_yrbf", "text": "the sum of their probabilities must be equal to one", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_12_C_j80z_nivi", "text": "their intersection must be zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_12_D_gb44_cyc8", "text": "None of these alternatives is correct.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_13_nv8b252", "text": "Two events, A and B, are mutually exclusive and each have a nonzero probability. If event A is known to occur, the probability of the occurrence of event B is", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_13_A_encn_lywr", "text": "one", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_13_B_evcd_uudo", "text": "any positive value", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_13_C_on2s_ezyd", "text": "zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_13_D_cwt7_snl8", "text": "any value between 0 to 1", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_14_03p8i6m", "text": "A numerical description of the outcome of an experiment is called a", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_14_A_vewy_12hf", "text": "descriptive statistic", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_14_B_qhwn_jy0z", "text": "probability function", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_14_C_560r_uvn4", "text": "variance", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_14_D_mt8i_vuii", "text": "random variable", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_15_81d1nkf", "text": "In the textile industry, a manufacturer is interested in the number of blemishes or flaws occurring in each 100 feet of material. The probability distribution that has the greatest chance of applying to this situation is the", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_15_A_2ocf_fbxz", "text": "normal distribution", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_15_B_l9cn_8u4z", "text": "binomial distribution", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_15_C_ckv8_0itp", "text": "Poisson distribution", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_15_D_se0l_qcfk", "text": "uniform distribution", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_16_uifo5wl", "text": "Which of the following is not a property of a binomial experiment?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_16_A_51q1_g8yt", "text": "the experiment consists of a sequence of n identical trials", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_16_B_9ltt_cb27", "text": "each outcome can be referred to as a success or a failure", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_16_C_f5xr_y6wr", "text": "the probabilities of the two outcomes can change from one trial to the next", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_16_D_g894_uo1n", "text": "the trials are independent", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_17_25jl6rj", "text": "The level of significance is the", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_17_A_mzgq_om3f", "text": "maximum allowable probability of Type II error", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_17_B_j0qv_guo1", "text": "maximum allowable probability of Type I error", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_17_C_6tzt_ux5c", "text": "same as the confidence coefficient", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_17_D_zuu8_edo7", "text": "same as the p-value", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019091_18_jny03wk", "text": "An important application of the chi-square distribution is", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019091_18_A_a5oc_8c06", "text": "making inferences about a single population variance", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_18_B_jb4b_sij2", "text": "testing for goodness of fit", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_18_C_hkzg_f8p1", "text": "testing for the independence of two variables", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019091_18_D_8j6v_m6bw", "text": "All of these alternatives are correct.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_19_elkgiwe", "text": "For a continuous random variable x, the probability density function f(x) represents", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_19_A_f6vf_ydcm", "text": "the probability at a given value of x", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_19_B_bbuy_ldii", "text": "the area under the curve at x", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_19_C_2hc6_aw60", "text": "the area under the curve to the right of x", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_19_D_ee5r_inef", "text": "the height of the function at x", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_20_rufgkqo", "text": "Convenience sampling is an example of", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_20_A_ht3f_9iq4", "text": "probabilistic sampling", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_20_B_nu8x_4wup", "text": "stratified sampling", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_20_C_361h_gi9q", "text": "nonprobabilistic sampling", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_20_D_87gl_n2ac", "text": "cluster sampling", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_21_e3vgtbl", "text": "In hypothesis testing, the hypothesis tentatively assumed to be true is", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_21_A_2oo4_czt3", "text": "the alternative hypothesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_21_B_seli_rgxe", "text": "the null hypothesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_21_C_otkx_s3yq", "text": "either the null or the alternative", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_21_D_7pg1_5gue", "text": "None of these alternatives is correct.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_22_oa055xr", "text": "In point estimation", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_22_A_6mrz_4yaz", "text": "data from the population is used to estimate the population parameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_22_B_7nke_zeep", "text": "data from the sample is used to estimate the population parameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_22_C_qqis_rbul", "text": "data from the sample is used to estimate the sample statistic", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_22_D_dw0i_x5or", "text": "the mean of the population equals the mean of the sample", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_23_kp6umqb", "text": "A variable that takes on the values of 0 or 1 and is used to incorporate the effect of qualitative variables in a regression model is called", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_23_A_tyia_iotg", "text": "an interaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_23_B_5q1a_zwxj", "text": "a constant variable", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_23_C_cau0_gcaf", "text": "a dummy variable", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_23_D_6zsn_x80n", "text": "None of these alternatives is correct.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_24_pzirbze", "text": "A property of a point estimator that occurs whenever larger sample sizes tend to provide point estimates closer to the population parameter is known as", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_24_A_8fcf_uxu8", "text": "efficiency", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_24_B_au4e_fh9r", "text": "unbiased sampling", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_24_C_goro_gwwa", "text": "consistency", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_24_D_1r6u_xqqp", "text": "relative estimation", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_25_ws13t9m", "text": "If a hypothesis is rejected at the 5% level of significance, it", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_25_A_xkpl_cqjl", "text": "will always be rejected at the 1% level", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_25_B_xl23_omdu", "text": "will always be accepted at the 1% level", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_25_C_1bpc_63vn", "text": "will never be tested at the 1% level", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_25_D_i8in_eb3m", "text": "may be rejected or not rejected at the 1% level", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_26_uv4jc8x", "text": "Which of the following does  not need to be known in order to compute the p-value?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_26_A_lzda_fryu", "text": "knowledge of whether the test is one-tailed or two-tailed", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_26_B_cv54_pnbl", "text": "the value of the test statistic", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_26_C_8a52_fvhz", "text": "the level of significance", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_26_D_2e9s_ylhh", "text": "None of these alternatives is correct.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_27_epte533", "text": "The ANOVA procedure is a statistical approach for determining whether or not", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_27_A_so83_3dec", "text": "the means of two samples are equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_27_B_kbm1_8o20", "text": "the means of two or more samples are equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_27_C_mihx_wgsr", "text": "the means of more than two samples are equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_27_D_l3e5_n3fc", "text": "the means of two or more populations are equal", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_28_19qa1zy", "text": "The range of the Durbin-Watson statistic is between", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_28_A_q1m2_om5e", "text": "1 to 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_28_B_s0wj_325l", "text": "0 to 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_28_C_5j4o_y044", "text": "infinity to + infinity", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_28_D_f4vh_3ik1", "text": "0 to 4", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_29_ymsvoe0", "text": "A random sample of 121 bottles of cologne showed an average content of 4 ounces. It is known that the standard deviation of the contents (i.e., of the population) is 0.22 ounces. In this problem the 0.22 is", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_29_A_th0h_ss88", "text": "a parameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_29_B_3slv_oj2k", "text": "a statistic", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_29_C_intl_yteq", "text": "the standard error of the mean", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_29_D_vvsf_z0ad", "text": "the average content of colognes in the long run", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_30_xlab9ar", "text": "Whenever using the t distribution in estimation, we must assume that", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_30_A_ifv5_hqj0", "text": "the sample size is at least 30", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_30_B_lg97_tzsl", "text": "the sampling distribution is approximately normal", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_30_C_976i_mx92", "text": "the population is approximately normal", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_30_D_elfa_lqfr", "text": "the finite population correction factor is necessary ", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_51_56abtex", "text": "In the market for magazines, the  income effect means that", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_51_A_95h6_c4mc", "text": "magazines are usually purchased by people with higher than average incomes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_51_B_ab79_5bu4", "text": "a decrease in the price of a substitute product like books will make magazine readers feel a little poorer than they were before.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_51_C_69h3_jc7v", "text": "an increase in the price of magazines will reduce the total purchasing power of magazine readers, making them able to afford fewer magazines.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_51_D_p2e7_huv6", "text": "an increase in the price of magazines will raise the relative price of magazines to books, causing magazine readers to read more books and fewer magazines.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_52_zsxm805", "text": "When the price of an inferior good falls,  ceteris paribus , the substitution effect leads to ________ in the quantity purchased and the income effect leads to ________ in the quantity purchased.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_52_A_h7ov_y4ks", "text": "an increase; an increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_52_B_qw6r_bzjg", "text": "an increase; a decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_52_C_udzc_b4ce", "text": "a decrease; an increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_52_D_1cxz_tw5a", "text": "a decrease; a decrease", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_53_1ludr18", "text": "The four parts of the business cycle occur in the following order:", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_53_A_53sp_8kzx", "text": "recession, trough, peak, expansion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_53_B_cexc_fg3x", "text": "expansion, trough, peak, recession.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_53_C_5rm7_744a", "text": "recession, trough, expansion, peak.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_53_D_85ze_vvgl", "text": "expansion, trough, recession, peak.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_54_feln1rs", "text": "Electric utility companies have built larger and larger electric generating stations and, as a result, the long - run average cost of producing each kilowatt hour decreased. This is an example of", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_54_A_rzex_mm93", "text": "constant returns to cost.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_54_B_qchu_g0lz", "text": "increasing returns to cost.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_54_C_gat0_c9nv", "text": "economies of scale.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_54_D_3m4d_smly", "text": "diseconomies of scale.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_55_ina7jpp", "text": "Suppose Sandy  Candies wants to increase its total re venues. If Sandy increases the price of her candy, she must be assuming that the demand for candy is", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_55_A_m5n2_bzek", "text": "unit elastic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_55_B_2h0r_dia1", "text": "inelastic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_55_C_ioq8_2pac", "text": "elastic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_55_D_t0m1_wwhz", "text": "income elastic.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_56_lten9x9", "text": "The above figures show the market for gasoline. Which figure shows the effect of a nation - wide strike by municipal bus drivers, which causes more people to drive their cars to work?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_56_A_jvpz_gw60", "text": "Figure A", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_56_B_llio_o74n", "text": "Figure B", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_56_C_7jef_l3dv", "text": "Figure C", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_56_D_buue_g0xl", "text": "Figure D", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_57_4l7wqxx", "text": "The above figures show the market for gasoline. Which figure(s) shows the effect of a new U.S. tax on oil that suppliers must pay?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_57_A_e6z7_0yyr", "text": "Figures A and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_57_B_wtep_wz4j", "text": "Figures B and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_57_C_b0gx_w2td", "text": "Figure A only", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_57_D_jqgd_ga3d", "text": "Figure C only", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_58_h38hhtf", "text": "The cost of inflation to society includes", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_58_A_2nvv_1g98", "text": "unpredictable changes in the value of money.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_58_B_pwv8_6407", "text": "higher interest rates paid by borrowers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_58_C_ifzj_oftz", "text": "higher interest rates paid by the government on its debt.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_58_D_7ao1_mv2h", "text": "the lost spending when people do not have enough money.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_59_ipq86g8", "text": "Which of the following pieces of information do you need to calculate the labor force participation rate? I. the number of employed persons II. the number of unemployed persons III. the population IV. the working age population", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_59_A_66ya_rqjx", "text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_59_B_mihp_xtq4", "text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_59_C_40qs_76j8", "text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_59_D_ah6n_lcjm", "text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_60_u9cvz80", "text": "Which of the following is the most liquid asset?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_60_A_pfc5_0wc3", "text": "money", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_60_B_sfkp_wj2p", "text": "land", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_60_C_443f_mqyd", "text": "a government bond", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_60_D_7c9h_ple6", "text": "a share of stock", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_61_o9ffech", "text": "If average variable cost is decreasing as output increases, then marginal cost is  definitely", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_61_A_8uov_e1sa", "text": "decreasing as output increases.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_61_B_c0l1_u9qh", "text": "increasing as output increases.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_61_C_jn2u_75qe", "text": "less than average variable cost.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_61_D_4spe_cnd3", "text": "greater than average variable cost.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_62_xqt8ei4", "text": "When all of the economy  resources are fully employed, the value of production is called", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_62_A_cp7g_7tdm", "text": "real GDP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_62_B_gdgl_y2mu", "text": "nominal GDP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_62_C_qm95_zzqn", "text": "actual GDP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_62_D_ylwd_nd9b", "text": "potential GDP.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_63_j1m4022", "text": "Which of the following is true regarding perfect competition? I. The firms are price takers. II. Marginal revenue equals the price of the product. III. Established firms have no advantage over new firms.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_63_A_7wf4_6s15", "text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_63_B_eqwm_o73b", "text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_63_C_o3vf_9arj", "text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_63_D_uvvb_z5iy", "text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_64_n5v56jo", "text": "If a perfectly competitive firm decides to shut down in the short run, its loss will equal its", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_64_A_klp1_yrrd", "text": "minimum average variable cost,  AVC .", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_64_B_53x1_f75t", "text": "total variable cost,  TVC .", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_64_C_c03g_sffa", "text": "total fixed cost,  TFC .", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_64_D_y3yj_fu0d", "text": "average total cost,  ATC .", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_65_kqcogg6", "text": "Patents encourage invention by", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_65_A_rpz8_km9m", "text": "offering subsidies to inventors.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_65_B_kfyo_ohji", "text": "offering tax breaks to inventors.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_65_C_29xn_9pqb", "text": "preventing others from copying an invention.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_65_D_03ng_2vsa", "text": "preventing inventors from working on the same project.", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_66_cklfad7", "text": "Which of the following is TRUE regarding job creation? I. The number of jobs created increases during an expansion. II. Job creation is fairly steady over the business cycle. III The number of jobs created decreases during a recession.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_66_A_3kuy_tn98", "text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_66_B_bfwd_aqqv", "text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_66_C_mvms_4hz9", "text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_66_D_ihc5_d0ft", "text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_67_xff10bz", "text": "Frictional unemployment comes about because of", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_67_A_kdgj_c0ku", "text": "friction between labor and management.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_67_B_rsfy_0w40", "text": "a mismatch between skills and available jobs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_67_C_n1n5_g67x", "text": "normal labor market turnover.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_67_D_kt9k_1klq", "text": "a general economic slowdown. 1", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_68_bbi1jxl", "text": "If the price level decreases and workers? money wage rates remain constant, which of the following will occur? I. The quantity of labor supplied will increase. II. The real wage rate will decrease. III. The labor supply curve will shift leftward.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_68_A_6vgx_lkzv", "text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_68_B_ydqe_7gcx", "text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_68_C_48yx_snao", "text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_68_D_yosg_yz2z", "text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_69_iivjir6", "text": "The real interest rate", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_69_A_wxc3_i9l0", "text": "can never be negative.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_B_0uhk_k2di", "text": "is approximately equal to the nominal interest rate plus the inflation rate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_C_zeb5_qtsg", "text": "is approximately equal to the nominal interest rate minus the inflation rate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_D_q6o3_wbqp", "text": "is positively related to the inflation rate. 20 Credit cards are", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_A_v43l_q2s1", "text": "a part of money because they are used in so many transactions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_B_h8a7_i5ik", "text": "a part of money when the transaction approach is used but not when the liquidity approach is used.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_C_iigo_tp1u", "text": "not part of money because they represent a loan of money to the user.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_69_D_bcug_drw3", "text": "not part of money because the government has no control over the amount of credit outstanding. II  ESSAY (50%)", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_75_5gva230", "text": "When considering outsourcing, what should firms be sure to avoid?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_75_A_4qpo_cjr9", "text": "Losing control of non-core activities which don  distinguish the firm.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_75_B_gzfz_6au3", "text": "Allowing outsourcing to develop into a substitute for innovation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_75_C_e3ju_pnqx", "text": "Giving the outsourcing partner the opportunity to become a strong competitor.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_75_D_pojx_iqvd", "text": "Allowing employees transferred to the outsourcing partner to rejoin the firm.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_75_E_7cku_uzfd", "text": "Adverse corporate tax implications of asset transfers to the outsourcing partner. (  )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_76_47wcxut", "text": "Which of the following statements is  TRUE ?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_76_A_qodp_g3u6", "text": "Maslow  hierarchy of needs started with belongingness, progressed to safety, and finally to esteem.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_76_B_nj4q_2e7d", "text": "McGregor believed that workers?motivation could be classified into one of two assumptions: Theory X workers and Theory Y workers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_76_C_fzgy_7hvg", "text": "Most early interpretations of the Hawthorne studies agreed that money was the cause of the increased output.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_76_D_4gsn_1i35", "text": "Bureaucratic Management theory was first described by Elton Mayo during the 1800s.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_76_E_yaso_2ycl", "text": "Henry Fayol suggested decisions based upon rule of thumb and tradition be replaced with more precise decisions and procedures developed after careful study of the situation. (  )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_77_h3or1vj", "text": "Which of the following statements is  FALSE ?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_77_A_x7s9_mdcj", "text": "Empowerment primarily means giving people power.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_77_B_ed7y_67iy", "text": "Corporate culture includes stories that keep an organization's values alive.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_77_C_4gu7_qum4", "text": "When goals are specific, measurable, challenging and linked to rewards, they are most effective.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_77_D_71l1_t1le", "text": "One of the problems with the MBO process is that strategic goals may be displaced by operational goals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_77_E_s9l4_k7ru", "text": "The purpose of horizontal communication is not only to inform but also to request support and cooperation. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_78_cloyu19", "text": "A successful dialogue requires that participants should", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_78_A_asoj_uo1u", "text": "actively persuade those they are communicating with.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_78_B_z4tg_f7v8", "text": "not deviate from the topic being deliberated.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_78_C_xpvp_i67r", "text": "remain firm and attached to a particular viewpoint.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_78_D_vnfv_b2q8", "text": "stay focused on their point of view only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_78_E_dt44_jjdo", "text": "talk openly to discover common ground. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_79_y75jwey", "text": "RFID (Radio Frequency Identification) chips: I. are used to track goods in distribution. II. are used to track job progress in production. III. may provide special instructions to operators. IV. can be used in inventory record keeping.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_79_A_9de5_pkxq", "text": "II and III only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_79_B_4xgq_03cw", "text": "I and II only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_79_C_swdv_9kk8", "text": "II, III, and IV.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_79_D_ulvl_gm0l", "text": "I, II, and IV.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_79_E_dl0p_gc17", "text": "IV only. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_80_0g87as9", "text": "ONE of the disadvantages of MBO is that:", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_80_A_j80o_nwz7", "text": "the process is very quick and informal.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_80_B_9nzr_rdsx", "text": "the process has no effect on worker commitment.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_80_C_h7ak_fxpq", "text": "the program only emphasizes what should be done in an organization.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_80_D_hitv_3uy6", "text": "carrying out the process is time consuming and requires additional paperwork.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_80_E_lx3m_kvbx", "text": "MBO duplicates other management practices. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_81_ytf3vlg", "text": "A group decision-making process which forbids negative feedback on any suggested alternative by any group member until all members have presented alternatives is known as:", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_81_A_zupa_xkqa", "text": "Groupthink.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_81_B_2rt7_nr69", "text": "Brainstorming.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_81_C_9f36_tvxi", "text": "the Delphi technique.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_81_D_obnj_oslp", "text": "the Nominal Group technique.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_81_E_u591_0xx3", "text": "the Devil  Advocate technique. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_82_quxsxx7", "text": "_______ imports develop when importers buy products from distributors in one country and sell them in another country to distributors who are not part of the manufacturer's regular distribution system.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_82_A_nli7_pbqq", "text": "Black-listed", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_82_B_edqt_b90h", "text": "Direct", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_82_C_j7nu_dn70", "text": "Circular", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_82_D_t9jx_3dac", "text": "Co-mingled", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_82_E_tjsp_k1rf", "text": "Parallel ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_83_8nfbcfv", "text": "Characteristics of the message itself help to determine its impact on attitudes. All of the following are issues that marketers are facing  EXCEPT for this one.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_83_A_kyac_o6k8", "text": "Should price be the prominent feature of any message?", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_B_zbql_2469", "text": "Should the message be conveyed in words or pictures?", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_C_81lb_uhew", "text": "How often should the message be repeated?", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_D_bxft_w1w3", "text": "Should both sides of an argument be presented?", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_E_a7pm_1z7g", "text": "Should the newest manufacturing procedures be adopted? (  ) 10.What is the major problem with Maslow Hierarchy of Needs in organizational behavior?", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_A_n754_1w8x", "text": "it is difficult to apply to the workplace", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_B_7v9s_lu0e", "text": "it is vague as to how a workplace can satisfy higher-order needs", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_C_fy8n_qfbk", "text": "its terminology tends to alienate those to whom it is applied", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_D_v12c_15zx", "text": "it is almost impossible to assess how well an individual has a particular need filled", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_83_E_s7c0_plvu", "text": "there is little evidence that needs are structured or operate in the way it describes (  )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_84_24llk6p", "text": "Performance evaluations are used as a mechanism for all of the following  EXECPT _____.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_84_A_6c3l_lzrg", "text": "monitoring the success of marketing strategies.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_84_B_t7d7_4fx2", "text": "determining promotions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_84_C_qf2k_iwuj", "text": "human resource planning.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_84_D_qo9l_c2fb", "text": "identifying training and development needs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_84_E_0l0s_autn", "text": "none of the above. (  )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_85_8r5glmi", "text": "What does an organization  NOT do to improve control?", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_85_A_ep7f_pz5t", "text": "Increase the number of managers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_85_B_ar49_i3q3", "text": "Increase the number of levels.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_85_C_woj0_v2dj", "text": "Increase the number of employees.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_85_D_uyxx_9msu", "text": "Make the hierarchy taller.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_85_E_12i3_6aj4", "text": "Decrease the span of control. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_86_hcugi3n", "text": "Coordination abilities refer to:", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_86_A_ka4c_apg1", "text": "the skills possessed by functional personnel.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_86_B_wg5p_8j77", "text": "the attributes that provide a competitive edge.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_86_C_c0wa_xtjj", "text": "planning the organization  strategy.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_86_D_qcjh_046r", "text": "linking functional and organizational resources.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_86_E_ydtc_eec2", "text": "improving organization  quality standard. ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_87_jj6q8bz", "text": "When a need is aroused that the consumer wishes to satisfy, the ________ process has been activated.", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_87_A_ffbl_wz1p", "text": "goals", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_87_B_juff_wq32", "text": "need", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_87_C_haax_ybln", "text": "desire", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_87_D_5fr8_al6m", "text": "motivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_87_E_6ua0_r7oq", "text": "vision ( )", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}, {"id": "q_1789319019092_88_66bndj6", "text": "Recent leadership theories such as charismatic and transformational leadership:", "type": "question", "image": null, "points": 1, "options": [{"id": "1789319019092_88_A_ehcm_x5zg", "text": "emphasize rational processes more than rational processes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_88_B_p41c_5ikt", "text": "emphasize emotional processes more than rational processes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_88_C_773q_u5xd", "text": "describe emotional and rational processes as equally important.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_88_D_jch4_xfmi", "text": "de-emphasized both rational and emotional processes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "1789319019092_88_E_cvqz_lkin", "text": "none of the above. II. Essay Questions", "isCorrect": false}], "explanation": "", "questionType": "Multiple Choice"}]}	["course_Licensure Examination for Professional Teachers (LEPT)", "batch_Batch 1 (2027)"]	\N	active	1	2026-09-13 22:30:20.725947+08	2026-09-14 01:08:52.911362+08
